 "speech_by": "claude",
 "speech": "Grizzly Rips, gather round. Sunday, October 18. Six wins, four losses, 41 goals scored and 25 let in. That's a B-minus, and I'll say it with my chest out, because y'all beat your usual by a country mile. We normally scratch out about 1.48 points a match. Today we hit 1.8. An 11-0 over Big Creamers, a 9-0 over fanum taxers, an 8-2 over Los Condenados. That's not winning, friends, that's a parade.\n\nNow the ladder. We woke up in Division 4, one win from Division 3 in our promotion series, and we're going to bed in exactly the same spot. Nothing moved. One match, one win, and we're through.\n\nHere's the honest part. We ran out of gas. 12 points in the first half of the session, 6 in the second, and we closed on three straight losses, ending with a 6-1 drubbing from La Tuna. We gave up 2.5 goals a match, and we got pantsed twice by four or more, including a 5-0 by YeskingFC. And we were forcing passes. Below about 72%, those extra balls start costing us. When nothing's on, keep it. Shield, turn back, let the shape reset. A sideways pass that keeps the ball beats a forward one that hands it over.\n\nPhogsToffees, you were a wildfire in a hay barn. 23 goals, 4 Man of the Match awards, a perfect 10.0 against FC Amarillo for your 5th Perfect Match with us, and 10 goals against Big Creamers. Ten! But against YeskingFC you vanished. 15 on-ball actions when you usually get 39. And when La Tuna went sideways, you quit. The best player on the pitch doesn't get to leave the pitch.\n\nBellyTb1, that perfect 10.0 against Los Condenados, 6 goal involvements in one match, was some of the prettiest football I've seen from you. 10 goals and 8 assists on the day. But your passing slid to 65%, down from your usual 75%, and against Big Creamers you put zero shots on target in an 11-0 rout. Then you walked out on La Tuna too. Simple pass first, and stay till the whistle.\n\nbuddskees, you're the glue. 62% of your tackles won, and a perfect 10.0 against Los Condenados, your 4th with us. Now, that red card against fanum taxers left us a player short for the rest of it, and you passed at 50% against Fish Academy. And I've got to ask: you rage quit an 11-0 win? Partner, that's like storming out of your own birthday party while they're bringing out the cake.\n\nThree rage quits today. Let's make tomorrow zero.\n\nHere's what I know, Grizzly Rips. A team that can score 11 can absolutely win 1. One match stands between us and Division 3, and I wouldn't trade this crew for all the sweet tea in Tennessee. Rest up, keep it simple, and let's go get that promotion together.",
